  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "driver-module",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/attachments.ts",
      "supports": "getAttachmentsForPlanPage and getAllAttachmentsForPlan validate the plan ID and place it as the only path segment of get_attachments_for_plan; the executor is declared with the attachments collection key and an envelope response, with request controls."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-paginated-list",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/paginated-list.ts",
      "supports": "The executor validates limit and offset before dispatch and appends them after the path. The page helper decodes with the strict page schema; the all helper copies only pageSize, startOffset, maxPages, maxItems, maxDurationMs and maxBytes from its options and runs collectAllPages with request controls."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-pagination",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/pagination.ts",
      "supports": "decodePage returns a bare array as a legacy-array page and an envelope with its offset, limit, size and _links. collectAllPages defaults pageSize to 250 and startOffset to 0, requires an envelope's offset to equal the offset it asked for, and ends at a legacy array or a null next link."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-url",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/url.ts",
      "supports": "buildEndpoint appends controls path-style after an ampersand, skips undefined values and percent-encodes each key and value."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-validation",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/validation.ts",
      "supports": "validateId accepts any positive integer: it tests Number.isInteger and has no safe-integer bound, so the largest-safe-integer ceiling on these identifiers is this server's own. validateEntryId accepts only a UUID, case-insensitively, with nothing before or after it; validatePaginationParams holds limit to 1..250 and offset to a non-negative integer."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-schema",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/schemas/attachments.ts",
      "supports": "AttachmentSchema is one passthrough object for every attachment shape TestRail documents: the upload reply, the legacy case and test entries, the plan, plan-entry and run entries with entity_attachments_id and icon_name, and the 7.1 cloud entries whose id is a UUID string. Every field is nullish and id and entity_id admit a number or a string, so each documented entity parses unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "testrail-attachments",
      "url": "https://support.testrail.com/hc/en-us/articles/7077196481428-Attachments",
      "supports": "get_attachments_for_plan/{plan_id} requires TestRail 6.3 or later and takes limit (250 by default) and offset on 6.7 or later. Its example is a bare array whose entity carries entity_attachments_id and icon_name and a null case_id. It answers 400 (described there as an invalid test ID) and 403 for no access or insufficient permissions."
    }
  ],
  "input_policy": {
    "ordinary_fields": "reject",
    "custom_fields": "reject",
    "notes": "Strictness is an MCP boundary requirement at every depth: the top level, query and _mcp are each closed. There are no filters; query carries only the paging controls."
  },
  "outer_result": {
    "driver": "page",
    "tool_data": "array",
    "notes": "Page mode returns the driver's decoded page, here a legacy-array page because the reference documents a bare array: the wrapper carries its entries as data and reports that no continuation is known. All mode returns the collected array, which a bare array ends. The reference also documents limit as the number of attachments the reply returns, so a bare array of exactly that size cannot be told from the end of the list. The driver decodes an envelope as well."
  },
